<!-- Project-specific / NestJS-Providers -->

### NestJS-Controllers

- Keep a controller to routing: take a validated DTO, call one service method, and return its result; never put a business rule in a controller.
- Never return a persistence entity from a controller, or accept one as its body type; map it to a DTO, so the wire format and the storage schema change independently.
<!-- Project-specific / NestJS-Controllers -->

### NestJS-Enhancers

- Keep each enhancer (guard, interceptor, pipe, or filter) to one job: a guard decides whether a request proceeds, an interceptor wraps the handler call, a pipe transforms or validates one argument, a filter maps an exception to a response; never put a business rule in one.
- Register each global enhancer once: in `main.ts`, or as an `APP_GUARD`, `APP_INTERCEPTOR`, `APP_PIPE`, or `APP_FILTER` provider when it needs injected dependencies, since one registered in `main.ts` can't inject any; never register an equivalent one in a feature module.
<!-- Project-specific / NestJS-Enhancers -->
